== 2. Pre-registration, verbatim ==
PRE-REGISTRATION: same-sitting head to head on the layer-overlap default, Ignition against AMD's Ryzen AI 1.7.1 stack.
Desktop 2 (DESKTOP-CBL5NUA, Phoenix), 2026-10-15. Written before any timed run. ignite-xdna main 653084f, Ignition
main 4f23442.

Arms, per model (two interleaved rounds, the second in reverse order):
- AMD: tools/amd_vitisai_yolo.py (YOLOv8n, YOLOv8s), tools/amd_vitisai_sesr.py (SESR M7), pipelines/yolov8n-pose/4_pose.py
  --ep npu (pose), resnet_env17, fresh cache keys compiled by an untimed run first.
- Ignition overlap: live_ignition.py on the default build (YOLOv8n/s and pose with --silu-sigmoid, as Ignition's docs
  build them; SESR M7 plain).
- Ignition barrier: the same build with --no-overlap-layers (the control that isolates the default's end-to-end effect).
50 warm-up + 500 timed frames of bus.jpg each, balanced power mode, xrt-smi idle before every run. Every Ignition
container verified layer-exact on the NPU first; a mismatch voids the sitting. Method as the v0.3.3 release sitting
(BENCHMARKS, 2026-09-17), which this re-runs.

Metric: glass-to-glass mean (ms) per run, as each tool prints it (for pose, AMD's arm is 4_pose.py's pre+infer+post,
as in the release sitting).

Predictions (orientation, from the dispatch A/B and the release sitting; not rules):
- overlap - barrier, per model: about the dispatch deltas (-1.00 / -1.31 / -1.14 / -0.08 ms).
- YOLOv8n and pose: Ignition faster than AMD (release: 8.50 vs 10.66, 9.28 vs 12.07).
- YOLOv8s: about level with AMD (release gap +1.4 ms, dispatch now -1.3 ms); sign not predicted.
- SESR M7: AMD faster (release 4.78 vs 4.35).

Rule for any doc that states who is faster on a model: "Ignition faster" only if the overlap arm's mean is below
AMD's in BOTH rounds; "AMD faster" only if above in both; otherwise "level within this sitting's spread".
A failed run, a busy NPU or a layer mismatch voids the sitting for that model.

